   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Free time, indoors and out",
     "texto": [
      "Today we talk about hobbies, games and shows.\n\n- **Hobbies:** **jardinería**, **bricolaje**, **crucigramas**. You can **coleccionar** **sellos** or **monedas**. If you like something a lot, you are «aficionado» to it.\n- **Going out:** having a picnic, going camping, sightseeing, going for tapas.\n- **Games:** a **juego de mesa** has a board, counters and a die. In a bar there are **dardos** and **billar**. With them you use **jugar a**.\n- **Sport:** a tennis **raqueta**, a football. The **chándal** is the clothing for sport.\n- **Shows:** at the box office you queue (**hacer cola**); on the ticket it says the **fila** and the seat. The spectators are the audience.\n- **On TV:** a series has episodes; for children there are cartoons."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Jugar a… and hacer…",
     "texto": [
      "With **jugar** you use **a** and the name of the game or sport:\n\n- **jugar a** los dardos · **jugar a** un juego de mesa\n- **jugar al** billar (**a + el = al**)\n\nThe verb **jugar** changes the **u** into **ue**: juego, juegas, juega, jugamos, jugáis, juegan.\n\nFor other hobbies you use **hacer**: **hacer** crucigramas, **hacer** bricolaje, **hacer** jardinería. And with **coleccionar** no preposition is needed: **coleccionar** sellos."
     ],
